IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc30-forms-preservation`
IMPORT `ccc30-forms-actors`

-- ccc30-tests-forms-preservation.l4 -- tests for ccc30-forms-preservation.l4 (Forms 5.001 to 5.0091, raw lines 17499-17719).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the Form's words. Where a date is "until (insert date)" the date inserted is 22 January 2026 in these tests.
-- A #TRACE prints its outcome and no assertion line, so each trace has its expected outcome written in the comment above it (read by eye) and the same duty
-- is asserted through the decision function over the facts.

§ `Tests -- Form 5.001, the preservation demand`

-- Duty to preserve: possession when received, until the date inserted, unless revoked or a document is obtained.
#ASSERT `form 5.001 the person is required to preserve the computer data` TRUE (Date 20 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the last day (the date read as inclusive: fork F-A) and the day after it
#ASSERT `form 5.001 the person is required to preserve the computer data` TRUE (Date 22 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.001 the person is required to preserve the computer data` TRUE (Date 23 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- data not in the person's possession or control when the demand was received
#ASSERT `form 5.001 the person is required to preserve the computer data` FALSE (Date 20 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "unless, before that date, this demand is revoked"
#ASSERT `form 5.001 the person is required to preserve the computer data` TRUE (Date 20 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "or a document that contains that data is obtained under a warrant or an order"
#ASSERT `form 5.001 the person is required to preserve the computer data` TRUE (Date 20 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- "If you contravene this demand without lawful excuse, you may be subject to a fine."
#ASSERT `form 5.001 contravening the demand without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to` TRUE FALSE `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 a fine` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the demand names a fine only: imprisonment, and both, are not stated
#ASSERT `form 5.001 contravening the demand without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to` TRUE FALSE `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 imprisonment` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.001 contravening the demand without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to` TRUE FALSE `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 both a fine and imprisonment` EQUALS NOTHING
-- a lawful excuse: the words "without lawful excuse" limit the sentence, so the case is not covered
#ASSERT `form 5.001 contravening the demand without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to` TRUE TRUE `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 a fine` EQUALS NOTHING
-- not contravened: the "If" is unmet
#ASSERT `form 5.001 contravening the demand without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to` FALSE FALSE `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 a fine` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Destruction, in accordance with section 487.0194 (the timing is outside the sources)
#ASSERT `form 5.001 the person is required to destroy` `forms 5.001 and 5.003 computer data that would not be retained in the ordinary course of business` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.001 the person is required to destroy` `forms 5.001 and 5.003 a document that is prepared for the purpose of preserving the computer data` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.001 the person is required to destroy` `forms 5.001 and 5.003 something else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "If you contravene that provision without lawful excuse, you may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both."
#ASSERT `form 5.001 contravening section 487.0194 without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to` TRUE FALSE `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 imprisonment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.001 contravening section 487.0194 without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to` TRUE FALSE `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 a fine` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.001 contravening section 487.0194 without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to` TRUE FALSE `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 both a fine and imprisonment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.001 contravening section 487.0194 without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to` TRUE TRUE `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 a fine` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.001 contravening section 487.0194 without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to` FALSE FALSE `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 a fine` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- Form 5.002, the 90 days requested`

-- "for 90 days after the day on which the order is made": the period in the text's unit, and as a date, on both sides of its end
#ASSERT (`form 5.002 the period requested`)'s days EQUALS 90
#ASSERT (`form 5.002 the period requested`)'s years EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`form 5.002 the period requested`)'s `less a day` EQUALS FALSE
-- an order made on 1 January 2026: 90 days after is 1 April 2026 (31 days of January, 28 of February, 31 of March, then 1 more)
#ASSERT `form 5.002 the last day of the period requested` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 1 4 2026
#ASSERT `form 5.002 the day is within the period requested` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.002 the day is within the period requested` (Date 2 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.002 the day is within the period requested` (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.002 the day is within the period requested` (Date 2 4 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a leap year (2028): 31 days of January, 29 of February, then 30 more days of March make 90, so the end is 31 March 2028
-- (the first draft of this expected value said 30 March: an addition slip by hand, caught by this assertion and recomputed by hand, not copied from the output)
#ASSERT `form 5.002 the last day of the period requested` (Date 1 1 2028) EQUALS Date 31 3 2028

§ `Tests -- Form 5.003, the preservation order`

#ASSERT `form 5.003 the person is required to preserve the specified computer data` TRUE (Date 20 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.003 the person is required to preserve the specified computer data` TRUE (Date 22 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.003 the person is required to preserve the specified computer data` TRUE (Date 23 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.003 the person is required to preserve the specified computer data` FALSE (Date 20 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.003 the person is required to preserve the specified computer data` TRUE (Date 20 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.003 the person is required to preserve the specified computer data` TRUE (Date 20 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.003 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.003 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.003 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.003 the person is required to destroy` `forms 5.001 and 5.003 computer data that would not be retained in the ordinary course of business` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.003 the person is required to destroy` `forms 5.001 and 5.003 a document that is prepared for the purpose of preserving the computer data` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.003 the person is required to destroy` `forms 5.001 and 5.003 something else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.003 contravening section 487.0194 without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.003 contravening section 487.0194 without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.003 contravening section 487.0194 without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- Form 5.0031, the 60 days requested`

#ASSERT (`form 5.0031 the period requested`)'s days EQUALS 60
-- 1 January 2026 plus 60 days is 2 March 2026 (31 + 28 = 59 days to the end of February, then 1 more day is 60: 1 January + 59 = 1 March, + 1 = 2 March)
#ASSERT `form 5.0031 the last day of the period requested` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 2 3 2026
#ASSERT `form 5.0031 the day is within the period requested` (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.0031 the day is within the period requested` (Date 3 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.0031 the day is within the period requested` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.0031 the day is within the period requested` (Date 2 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- leap year: 1 January 2028 plus 60 days is 1 March 2028
#ASSERT `form 5.0031 the last day of the period requested` (Date 1 1 2028) EQUALS Date 1 3 2028

§ `Tests -- Form 5.0032, the keep account open or active order`

#ASSERT `form 5.0032 para (a) the person is required to keep the specified account open or active` (Date 20 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.0032 para (a) the person is required to keep the specified account open or active` (Date 22 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.0032 para (a) the person is required to keep the specified account open or active` (Date 23 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "unless the holder of the account requests that you close or deactivate it"
#ASSERT `form 5.0032 para (a) the person is required to keep the specified account open or active` (Date 20 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "or this order is revoked or varied"
#ASSERT `form 5.0032 para (a) the person is required to keep the specified account open or active` (Date 20 1 2026) (Date 22 1 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.0032 para (b) the person is required to notify the peace officer or public officer` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.0032 para (b) the person is required to notify the peace officer or public officer` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.0032 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.0032 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.0032 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- Form 5.004, which standard of grounds the information states`

#ASSERT `form 5.004 the standard of grounds the information states` `form 5.004 section 487.014` EQUALS JUST `form 5.004 reasonable grounds to believe`
#ASSERT `form 5.004 the standard of grounds the information states` `form 5.004 section 487.0141` EQUALS JUST `form 5.004 reasonable grounds to believe`
#ASSERT `form 5.004 the standard of grounds the information states` `form 5.004 section 487.015` EQUALS JUST `form 5.004 reasonable grounds to suspect`
#ASSERT `form 5.004 the standard of grounds the information states` `form 5.004 section 487.016` EQUALS JUST `form 5.004 reasonable grounds to suspect`
#ASSERT `form 5.004 the standard of grounds the information states` `form 5.004 section 487.017` EQUALS JUST `form 5.004 reasonable grounds to suspect`
#ASSERT `form 5.004 the standard of grounds the information states` `form 5.004 section 487.018` EQUALS JUST `form 5.004 reasonable grounds to suspect`
#ASSERT `form 5.004 the standard of grounds the information states` `form 5.004 another section` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- Forms 5.005, 5.0051, 5.006, 5.007 and 5.008, producing the document`

-- Form 5.005: within the time allowed (30 days here), at the place and in the form stated
#ASSERT `form 5.005 the document was produced as the order requires` 30 30 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.005 the document was produced as the order requires` 30 31 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.005 the document was produced as the order requires` 30 0 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.005 the document was produced as the order requires` 30 10 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.005 the document was produced as the order requires` 30 10 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.005 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.005 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.005 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Form 5.0051: "(specify up to six dates)", and the time of each date
#ASSERT `form 5.0051 the number of dates specified is within the limit` 6 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.0051 the number of dates specified is within the limit` 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.0051 the number of dates specified is within the limit` 7 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.0051 the number of dates specified is within the limit` 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.0051 the document was produced as the order requires after a date specified` 10 10 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.0051 the document was produced as the order requires after a date specified` 10 11 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.0051 the document was produced as the order requires after a date specified` 10 5 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.0051 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.0051 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.0051 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Form 5.006: "on being served ... in accordance with subsection 487.015(4)", then "as soon as feasible"
#ASSERT `form 5.006 the person is ordered to prepare and produce the document` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.006 the person is ordered to prepare and produce the document` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.006 the person is ordered to prepare and produce the document` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.006 the document was produced as the order requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.006 the document was produced as the order requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.006 the document was produced as the order requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.006 the document was produced as the order requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.006 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.006 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.006 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Forms 5.007 and 5.008: within (time) at (place) in (form), and the contravention sentence
#ASSERT `form 5.007 the document was produced as the order requires` 14 14 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.007 the document was produced as the order requires` 14 15 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.007 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.007 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.007 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.008 the document was produced as the order requires` 7 7 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.008 the document was produced as the order requires` 7 8 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.008 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.008 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.008 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The production duty as a regulative rule, with the time allowed (30 days) as the input. The clock counts days from receipt of the order (AT 0).
-- Expected from the text ("must be produced ... within (time)"): produced at day 10 -> FULFILLED; produced at day 30 (the last day) -> FULFILLED;
-- produced at day 31, or never -> BREACH.
#TRACE `form 5.005 the person must produce the document` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `forms 1 to 23 the person to whom the demand, order or summons is addressed` DOES `form 5.005 produces the document to the peace officer or public officer` AT 10

#TRACE `form 5.005 the person must produce the document` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `forms 1 to 23 the person to whom the demand, order or summons is addressed` DOES `form 5.005 produces the document to the peace officer or public officer` AT 30

#TRACE `form 5.005 the person must produce the document` 30 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 31

#TRACE `form 5.005 the person must produce the document` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `forms 1 to 23 the person to whom the demand, order or summons is addressed` DOES `form 5.005 produces the document to the peace officer or public officer` AT 31

§ `Tests -- Forms 5.0032 to 5.0091, the right to apply to revoke or vary`

#ASSERT `forms 5.0032 to 5.0091 the person has the right to apply to revoke or vary the order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "You" is the addressee: another person is not covered, which is not the same as having no right
#ASSERT `forms 5.0032 to 5.0091 the person has the right to apply to revoke or vary the order` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- Form 5.0091, the non-disclosure order`

-- "during a period of (identify the period) after the day on which this order is made": 30 days from an order made on 1 January 2026 ends on 31 January 2026
#ASSERT `form 5.0091 the person is prohibited from disclosing on the day` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 30 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.0091 the person is prohibited from disclosing on the day` (Date 2 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.0091 the person is prohibited from disclosing on the day` (Date 31 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.0091 the person is prohibited from disclosing on the day` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 30 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 5.0091 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 5.0091 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 5.0091 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The prohibition as a regulative rule (SHANT with a WITHIN that sunsets), the period being 30 days counted from the day of the order (AT 0).
-- Expected from the text: disclosure at day 10 (inside the period) -> BREACH; disclosure at day 40 (after the period) -> FULFILLED; no disclosure -> FULFILLED.
#TRACE `form 5.0091 the person must not disclose` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `forms 1 to 23 the person to whom the demand, order or summons is addressed` DOES `form 5.0091 discloses the existence of the demand or order` AT 10

#TRACE `form 5.0091 the person must not disclose` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `forms 1 to 23 the person to whom the demand, order or summons is addressed` DOES `form 5.0091 discloses the existence of the demand or order` AT 40

#TRACE `form 5.0091 the person must not disclose` 30 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 40
